# PIPE: the PASSABLE PIPE's test course (SPEC.md 130.12.3.6) - not shipped, on no disk, in no tour: compiled by
# `bbcourse.py --selfcheck`'s section `pipeunder` and by tests/bonanza_phys.py's pipe scenes (the guest's archway
# part against the model).  Two KEEP tubes across the floor, each with its two end legs walls one unit over the
# floor and its middle leg a pipe hanging `column 1` deep over the floor with room for the ball under it:
#   A (row 8):  the middle at 5 units, its underside 4 - two units over the floor, the clearance 0: the ball ROLLS
#               under it and a Hop or a boost into it is stopped at its face
#   B (row 14): the middle at 6 units, its underside 5 - three units over the floor, the clearance 8 px: rubber's
#               Hop (5.7 px) passes under it and its boost (9.3 px) hits the underside
course PIPE "Pipe underpass"
width 96
origin 352
ball rubber
music fairway
uses tube archway
floor rect 4 4 24 20 flat 2
tube keep 6 8 16 8 via 9 8 via 13 8 body 3 5 3 column 1
tube keep 6 14 16 14 via 9 14 via 13 14 body 3 6 3 column 1
start 5 5
goal rect 22 18 24 20 flat 2
clock 21 17
target 60
way 5 5
way 23 19
